  "party_positions": [
    {
      "claims": [
        {
          "attribution": "Lucky Brand Dungarees, Inc.",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "11b7eb020fd6053d75e88a358f616f64886177670403973c907aa95eeb78d4ef",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-11b7eb020fd6-0000-0001"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 4,
                "start": 4
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Lucky Brand Dungarees, Inc., petitioner argues the Court should reverse the Second Circuit because it erred in holding that a defense never previously litigated to judgment can be barred when new claims arise."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Lucky Brand Dungarees, Inc.",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "11b7eb020fd6053d75e88a358f616f64886177670403973c907aa95eeb78d4ef",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-11b7eb020fd6-0000-0002"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 5,
                "start": 5
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Lucky Brand Dungarees, Inc., petitioner clarifies it is not arguing that defenses can never be barred; issue preclusion may bar a previously resolved defense, and unresolved defenses cannot be raised in a judgment enforcement action or in a collateral attack on a prior judgment."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Lucky",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "11b7eb020fd6053d75e88a358f616f64886177670403973c907aa95eeb78d4ef",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-11b7eb020fd6-0001-0002"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 24,
                "start": 24
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Lucky, petitioner explains the settlement agreement required Lucky to stop using the phrase \u201cGet Lucky,\u201d but that trademarks containing \u201cLucky\u201d that were used before the settlement are extinguished."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Lucky",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "11b7eb020fd6053d75e88a358f616f64886177670403973c907aa95eeb78d4ef",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-11b7eb020fd6-0001-0003"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 25,
                "start": 25
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Lucky, petitioner states the settlement does not prevent the use of the \u201cGet Lucky\u201d trademark."
        }
      ],
      "heading": "Petitioner \u2013 Lucky Brand Dungarees, Inc.",
      "status": "complete",
      "summary": null,
      "summary_citations": []
    },
    {
      "claims": [
        {
          "attribution": "Mr. Kimberly",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "11b7eb020fd6053d75e88a358f616f64886177670403973c907aa95eeb78d4ef",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-11b7eb020fd6-0002-0000"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 44,
                "start": 44
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Mr. Kimberly, respondent argues that failure to raise a defense in a prior action can bar raising that defense in later actions."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Mr. Kimberly",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "11b7eb020fd6053d75e88a358f616f64886177670403973c907aa95eeb78d4ef",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-11b7eb020fd6-0002-0001"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 45,
                "start": 45
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Mr. Kimberly, respondent relies on the City of Beloit case (1968) to support its proposition."
        }
      ],
      "heading": "Respondent \u2013 Marcel Fashions Group, Inc.",
